{ CommCtrl - comctl32 bindings: InitCommonControlsEx, image lists, and the class names, styles, messages, notification
  codes and records of the tab, status bar, tool bar, progress, track bar, list view, tree view, tooltip, up-down and
  header controls (rtl/winapi.md sections 1 and 5.5; task R-112). Uses Windows and Messages (WM_USER).
  Written by hand from the Win32 reference on learn.microsoft.com (RTL-800):
  - the reference page of every comctl32 function declared below (InitCommonControlsEx, ImageList_* in
    commctrl.h, among them ImageList_Replace and ImageList_SetOverlayImage, task R-249, and ImageList_GetBkColor,
    task R-253) and the ImageList_AddIcon
    and INDEXTOOVERLAYMASK macro pages;
  - the DRAWITEMSTRUCT structure page (ODT_TAB, task R-255; the page names the constant without its number: 101 is
    the value of the Win32 API metadata published by Microsoft with its windows-rs project (MIT licence), a fact only);
  - the structure pages INITCOMMONCONTROLSEX, NMCUSTOMDRAW, NMLVCUSTOMDRAW, NMTVCUSTOMDRAW, TCITEMW,
    TCHITTESTINFO, TBBUTTON, TBADDBITMAP, TBBUTTONINFOW, NMTOOLBARW, PBRANGE, UDACCEL, NMUPDOWN, TTTOOLINFOW,
    NMTTDISPINFOW, HDITEMW, HDLAYOUT, HDHITTESTINFO, NMHEADERW, LVITEMW, LVCOLUMNW, NMLISTVIEW, NMITEMACTIVATE,
    NMLVDISPINFOW, LVHITTESTINFO, LVFINDINFOW, TVITEMW, TVITEMEXW, TVINSERTSTRUCTW, NMTREEVIEWW, NMTVDISPINFOW,
    TVHITTESTINFO, TVSORTCB, NMLVKEYDOWN, NMTVKEYDOWN, NMTCKEYDOWN (the last three 1-byte packed, RTL-831);
  - the "Common Control Window Classes", "Common Control Styles", "Common Control Notifications" (NM_*), "Custom
    Draw" and "Image List Draw Flags" pages, and per control the "<control> Control Styles", "<control> Messages",
    "<control> Notifications" and extended-style pages.
  Only the W variants are declared (RTL-821); each W message, notification and record also has its unsuffixed alias.
  Notification codes are negative in C; they are declared as UINT values, the type of TNMHdr.code.
  INITCOMMONCONTROLSEX has no upper-case alias (it would equal the function InitCommonControlsEx).
  Unions are declared as one member padded to the union's size (RTL-833): TTVInsertStructW holds item
  (TVITEMW) and pads to the size of TVITEMEXW. LPSTR_TEXTCALLBACKW is an inline function: an ordinal-to-pointer
  cast is not a constant expression (LANG-340). }
